  "matched_pilot_scope": "S3 parent 100k and S0 parent 50k; fresh optimizer with common 1e-5 LR. Compare within architecture only. Full runs use original generic initialization, not these mature checkpoints.",
  "reasons": [
    "TTC improves on full held-out dev in both architectures with log-cluster 95% intervals above zero.",
    "S0 collision score improves with a positive log-cluster interval; zero scenes fall from 83 to 65.",
    "Full-dev progress changes are small (-0.0373 points S3, -0.0721 S0); no material nominal PDMS sacrifice.",
    "Four-seed S3 PDMS change is positive at every seed; braking-scene mean-trajectory velocity and longitudinal errors improve in both architectures on the fixed diagnostic subset.",
    "Original 8-GPU V12 runtime is finite and updates real FP32 masters, with median steps approximately 1.7 seconds."
  ],
  "tradeoffs_and_limits": [
    "Overall single-seed ADE worsens: S3 0.7160 to 0.7377 m, S0 0.7708 to 0.8409 m; do not call this a universal fitting improvement.",
    "Repeated-noise position RMS increases: S3 0.1025 to 0.1775 m, S0 0.1947 to 0.2947 m; no stability improvement demonstrated.",
    "Full-dev aggregate PDMS confidence intervals overlap zero for both architectures.",
    "The 128-scene four-seed S0 PDMS delta is -0.1084 points with a wide interval; S3 zero cases increase from 16 to 18.",
    "S3 full-dev braking positive overshoot p95 slightly worsens (4.6557 to 4.7743 m), although repeated-mean braking diagnostics improve.",
    "Braking reweighting uses a GT speed-drop proxy, not an actor-risk or certified perturbation label.",
    "Short mature-checkpoint adaptation and V12 runtime checks cannot establish from-scratch 100k gains.",
    "V12 full-run performance is unmeasured; direct GT safety checks and real dataset/8-GPU runtime are qualified."
  ],
